## Judgements (auditor)
- D-088..D-116 (plan, worktree waves, integration edits, disclosed limitations): each limitation is disclosed in the register notes (e.g. REQ-PB-066/REQ-S15-008 API clock not settable; REQ-PB-065/REQ-S04-014/REQ-S07-015 stub + integration only; REQ-S04-010 409 not 422; REQ-S08-006 rates as formula variables) and none hides a failed mandatory acceptance criterion; acceptable as disclosed, as judged in round 8 on identical product code and register (register unchanged since).
- D-117/D-119/D-122: every round 1-3 finding repaired, none accepted; the value-basis rule (profit-and-cash gross; revenue_uplift and avoided_cost separate; per-basis gaps, worst-of RAG) was accepted by the round-2 and round-3 domain reviewers against M0172/B0145 (D-119, D-122), so neither 'Reopen if' fallback fired.
- D-123..D-126: round-3 repairs and the D-124 defects (see 05-incidents-salvage.log) are in the candidate.
- D-127..D-130: F-DG4-143/144 repaired, not accepted (D-127); FE-R9 kill salvaged by FE-R9B (05 log).
- D-131..D-135: F-DG4-128 a real defect, repaired and verified; F-DG4-148 put to the user, accepted with the envelope (D-134); round 8 confirmation.
- D-136: claims verified independently (04 log): 33 files restored, 360 identical pairs, checkWriteOnce 0 (99 before), frozen_at equal rounds 1-9, B1 holds (decisions.md untouched after f2ae717), B2 imported.
